    </div>

    <p>The format is available for immediate adoption. No registration, no application, no gate. Take the specification, structure your work to it, and attribute the genesis block. The standard grows; the origin is permanent.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <span class="section-label">06 — In Practice</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading">Testing the Architecture with Google NotebookLM</h2>
    <p>The most immediate demonstration of the Living Document Specification's performance advantage is Google NotebookLM — a platform that allows users to upload documents and interact with them via AI. A book written to the specification performs qualitatively differently from a standard linear document in this environment.</p>
    <p>Because NotebookLM parses structural landmarks, the explicit layer headers — Value Layer, Deep Dive Layer, Business Hook Layer, Metadata Layer — function as navigation anchors. The platform segments data blocks cleanly. Audio overviews automatically adopt the framing structures declared in the document. Prompts that would require inference from a flat text file resolve precisely from a structured one.</p>
    <p>The first book published under this specification is <em>Beyond AI Disruption</em>. Upload it to NotebookLM and prompt: "Pull all Business Hook Layers and compile them into an executive audit checklist." The output demonstrates the architecture more clearly than any description of it can.</p>
